  "finalText": "I built the toggle in the open comp, and the contact sheet shows it working across the six frames I checked. It starts off and grey, and the toggle begins at 0.4s. By 0.9s it's on and green with the checkmark showing, and it settles by 1.1s.\n\n- **Track:** a grey pill whose fill crossfades to iOS green between 0.4s and 0.8s.\n- **Knob:** a white circle with a soft shadow. It slides right and overshoots by about 9px at 0.72s, then eases back into place by 1.1s.\n- **Squash and stretch:** the knob stretches to 120% × 90% mid-travel and compresses to 92% × 108% as it lands.\n- **Checkmark:** green, inside the knob so it travels with it. It draws on from 0.7s to 1.0s as the knob arrives.\n\nI used one easing family (Cubic) throughout. I can make it bouncier, add a press-down squash before the move, or make the toggle loop back off."
